# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows checks files out with CRLF by default (core.autocrlf=true).
# For a shell script copied into a Linux image that is fatal but baffling: the
# kernel reads the shebang as "/bin/sh\r", cannot find an interpreter by that
# name, and reports "no such file or directory" - about a file that plainly
# exists. Pin every script to LF so a Windows checkout produces the same bytes
# the container expects.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read by Linux tooling, never by Windows.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
